 "function": "cloudgen.noise.octave_ladder",
 "doc": "hi / low is EXACTLY lacunarity^3, so the floor of ln(ratio) / ln(lacunarity) sits on the integer 3: with lacunarity 2 numpy gives 3.0 (n = 4, start 1) but with 2.03 it gives 2.9999999999999996 (n = 3, start 2.03, although four octaves 1, 2.03, 4.12, 8.37 fit). The result depends on how ln rounds, so another math library can land on the other side. Tagged fragile: it pins the Python result. n exact, start float64 closed form (rtol 1e-9).",
